{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "54a504f9-c46a-4728-9e63-1aa434ce2d28",
    "name": "EventHubAPI - Data-Driven",
    "description": "## EventHubAPI – Data-Driven Testing\n\nThis collection validates the **EventHub API** using a **data-driven testing approach**, where multiple sets of input values are fed through a single collection run to maximize coverage with minimal repetition.\n\nEach folder in this collection targets a specific resource or workflow. Requests are driven by **Postman Datasets** — a first-class Postman entity for tabular data — allowing the same test logic to execute repeatedly across different input rows in one run. Each row in a dataset becomes an iteration, feeding variable values directly into requests, scripts, and assertions.\n\nThis approach makes it easy to:\n\n- Cover a wide range of scenarios (happy path, negative and edge cases) without duplicating requests\n    \n- Catch regressions across any EventHub API endpoint\n    \n- Confirm consistent API behaviour across varied data sets\n    \n\n---\n\n### Notes:\n\n- A total of **6 failed test assertions** have been identified to date.\n    \n- The identified failures are attributed to **BUG-001 and BUG-005**, as documented in the **Bug Reports** collection.\n    \n- The response time test assertion may fail when the response time exceeds **2,000 ms**.\n    \n\n---\n\n### Structure\n\nFolders are organized by resource and workflow. Each folder maps to a Postman Dataset that supplies the variable values for that run:\n\n| Folder | Resource | Dataset |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Events > Events – CRUD | Events | Data-Driven Events – CRUD |\n\n> More folders and datasets will be added here as coverage expands to other EventHub API resources. \n  \n\n### When to use\n\nRun this collection (or individual folders) with the linked Postman Dataset selected in the Collection Runner whenever you need to:\n\n- Validate API behaviour across multiple input scenarios in a single pass\n    \n- Catch regressions introduced by changes to any EventHub endpoint\n    \n- Confirm data integrity across full resource lifecycles (create → read → update → delete)\n    \n\n---",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "54248427"
  },
